RK3588-LinuxCNC — 3-axis EtherCAT milling machine configuration
================================================================

This is a REAL HARDWARE config for:
  - Board:   Vanxak HD-RK3588-CORE (RK3588J, PREEMPT_RT)
  - Drives:  3x SSDC06-ECX-H (Shanghai AMP/MOONS' step-servo, CiA402)
  - EtherCAT: IgH master via ec_generic on end0
  - GUI:     gmoccapy

Files:
  rk3588-linuxcnc.ini   Main INI (axes, kinematics, GUI)
  ethercat-conf.xml     lcec EtherCAT slave config (3x basic_cia402, CSP)
  core_lcec.hal         Core HAL: lcec + motmod + scale (mm<->counts)
  home.hal              Limit/home switch wiring from drive digital inputs
  estop.hal             E-stop loopback (TODO: real E-stop chain)
  spindle_sim.hal       Simulated spindle (TODO: real VFD)
  postgui.hal           Post-GUI HAL (spindle feedback, tool offsets)
  tool.tbl              Tool table
  rk3588.var            G-code parameters
  position.txt          Last position

TODO before first run (adjust to your machine):
  1. Motor encoder resolution:  ethercat-conf.xml encoderRatio + INI INPUT_SCALE
     - AMxxSS-N motors: 20000 counts/rev (default)
     - AMxxRS motors:   4096 counts/rev
  2. Leadscrew pitch:  ethercat-conf.xml feedRatio + INI INPUT_SCALE
     - 1610 (10 mm/rev) + 4096 enc => 409.6 counts/mm (current X)
  3. Travel limits:  INI [AXIS_*] MIN/MAX_LIMIT + ethercat-conf.xml positionLimitMin/Max
  4. Home method/velocity:  ethercat-conf.xml homeMethod, homeVelocityFast/Slow
  5. Drive digital input mapping:  use Stepper Suite to map physical inputs
     to positive-limit / negative-limit / home functions (0x60FD)
  6. E-stop:  replace estop.hal loopback with real E-stop chain
  7. Spindle:  replace spindle_sim.hal with real VFD control

EtherCAT bring-up:
  systemctl start ethercat        # start IgH master
  ethercat master                 # check Phase: Idle, slaves detected
  ethercat slaves                 # list slaves
  ethercat pdos                   # check PDO mapping

Start LinuxCNC:
  linuxcnc /home/root/linuxcnc/configs/rk3588-linuxcnc/rk3588-linuxcnc.ini
